[2026-03-14T21:51:43.082Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011UTLAeEMSfxZJf7RbAo4o1","type":"tool_result","content":"   835→### TeamFilters\n   836→\n   837→#### Test: Team filters toolbar renders with all filter options\n   838→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/team/eng-1/issues`\n   839→- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the issue list displays filter controls: \"Status\", \"Priority\", \"Assignee\", \"Label\", \"Project\", and \"Cycle\" filters. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a dropdown.\n   840→\n   841→#### Test: Status filter dropdown shows all statuses with icons\n   842→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   843→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" filter button\n   844→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all statuses: Backlog (dotted circle, gray), Todo (circle, gray), In Progress (half circle, yellow), In Review (three-quarter circle, blue), Done (check circle, green), Cancelled (x-circle, red). Each option has a checkbox.\n   845→\n   846→#### Test: Status filter filters issues by selected statuses\n   847→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues in Backlog (3), In Progress (2), Done (1)\n   848→- **Action**: User opens the Status filter and selects only \"In Progress\"\n   849→- **Expected**: Only the \"In Progress\" group is displayed with its 2 issues. Backlog and Done groups are hidden. The Status filter button shows a visual indicator that a filter is active.\n   850→\n   851→#### Test: Priority filter dropdown shows all priorities with icons\n   852→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   853→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Priority\" filter button\n   854→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing: Urgent (alert-triangle, red), High (arrow-up, orange), Medium (minus, yellow), Low (arrow-down, blue), No Priority (dots-horizontal, gray). Each option has a checkbox.\n   855→\n   856→#### Test: Priority filter filters issues by selected priorities\n   857→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with priorities High (2), Medium (1), Low (1)\n   858→- **Action**: User opens Priority filter and selects \"High\"\n   859→- **Expected**: Only issues with High priority are displayed across all status groups. Issues with Medium and Low priority are hidden.\n   860→\n   861→#### Test: Assignee filter dropdown shows all team members\n   862→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team \"Engineering\" has members Alice, Bob, and Charlie\n   863→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Assignee\" filter button\n   864→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all team members with their avatars and names: Alice, Bob, Charlie, and an \"Unassigned\" option. Each option has a checkbox.\n   865→\n   866→#### Test: Assignee filter filters issues by selected assignees\n   867→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (Alice), ENG-2 (Bob), ENG-3 (Alice), ENG-4 (unassigned)\n   868→- **Action**: User opens Assignee filter and selects \"Alice\"\n   869→- **Expected**: Only issues assigned to Alice are shown (ENG-1 and ENG-3). Issues assigned to Bob and unassigned issues are hidden.\n   870→\n   871→#### Test: Label filter dropdown shows all available labels\n   872→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has labels \"Bug\" (red), \"Feature\" (green), \"Improvement\" (blue)\n   873→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Label\" filter button\n   874→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all workspace labels with their colored dots and names. Each option has a checkbox.\n   875→\n   876→#### Test: Label filter filters issues by selected labels\n   877→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (labeled \"Bug\"), ENG-2 (labeled \"Feature\"), ENG-3 (labeled \"Bug\", \"Feature\")\n   878→- **Action**: User opens Label filter and selects \"Bug\"\n   879→- **Expected**: Only issues with the \"Bug\" label are shown (ENG-1 and ENG-3). ENG-2 is hidden.\n   880→\n   881→#### Test: Project filter dropdown shows all team projects\n   882→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has projects \"Auth Rewrite\" and \"Dashboard v2\"\n   883→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Project\" filter button\n   884→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing \"Auth Rewrite\", \"Dashboard v2\", and a \"No Project\" option. Each has a checkbox.\n   885→\n   886→#### Test: Project filter filters issues by selected projects\n   887→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (project \"Auth Rewrite\"), ENG-2 (project \"Dashboard v2\"), ENG-3 (no project)\n   888→- **Action**: User opens Project filter and selects \"Auth Rewrite\"\n   889→- **Expected**: Only ENG-1 is shown. ENG-2 and ENG-3 are hidden.\n   890→\n   891→#### Test: Cycle filter dropdown shows team cycles\n   892→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has cycles \"Sprint 1\" (active), \"Sprint 2\" (upcoming)\n   893→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cycle\" filter button\n   894→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing \"Sprint 1\", \"Sprint 2\", and a \"No Cycle\" option. The active cycle is visually indicated. Each option has a checkbox.\n   895→\n   896→#### Test: Cycle filter filters issues by selected cycle\n   897→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (in \"Sprint 1\"), ENG-2 (in \"Sprint 1\"), ENG-3 (no cycle)\n   898→- **Action**: User opens Cycle filter and selects \"Sprint 1\"\n   899→- **Expected**: Only issues in Sprint 1 are shown (ENG-1 and ENG-2). ENG-3 is hidden.\n   900→\n   901→#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n   902→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (High priority, Bug label, In Progress), ENG-2 (High priority, Feature label, In Progress), ENG-3 (Low priority, Bug label, Backlog)\n   903→- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter and \"Bug\" in Label filter\n   904→- **Expected**: Only ENG-1 is shown (matches both High priority AND Bug label). ENG-2 and ENG-3 are hidden.\n   905→\n   906→#### Test: Clearing a filter restores all issues\n   907→- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\" only, showing 2 issues out of 6 total\n   908→- **Action**: User opens Status filter and deselects \"In Progress\" (or clicks a \"Clear\" option)\n   909→- **Expected**: All 6 issues are shown again across all status groups, same as the unfiltered view.\n   910→\n   911→#### Test: Filter state shows active filter indicators\n   912→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, no filters applied\n   913→- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter\n   914→- **Expected**: The Priority filter button shows a visual indicator that it is active (e.g., highlighted background, badge showing \"1\", or different styling). Other filter buttons remain in their default/inactive state.\n   915→\n   916→#### Test: Filters can be used repeatedly after clearing\n   917→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated with multiple issues at various statuses and priorities\n   918→- **Action**: User applies Priority filter for \"High\", clears it, then applies Assignee filter for \"Alice\", clears it, then applies Status filter for \"Done\"\n   919→- **Expected**: Each filter application and clearing works correctly. After the final action, only \"Done\" issues are shown. All filter controls remain responsive and functional through multiple interactions.\n   920→\n   921→#### Test: Filters work correctly with grouping options\n   922→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issues grouped by Priority, Assignee filter set to \"Alice\"\n   923→- **Expected**: Only Alice's issues are shown, grouped under their respective priority headers. Empty priority groups (where Alice has no issues) are not displayed.\n   924→\n   925→#### Test: Filters persist while navigating withi